      "info": {
        "title": "3ds-recorder",
        "author": "BolgarMaxym97",
        "description": "Record your whole Nintendo 3DS screen — games, HOME Menu and apps, both screens with sound — with a Luma3DS sysmodule. Converts recordings to MP4 on the console and sends them to your phone over Wi-Fi via QR code. Old & New 3DS.",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "v1.7.0",
        "license": "MIT",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-23 at 20:23 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "v1.7.0 (2026-11-23)\n3DS Recorder 1.7.0 updates itself: from now on a new version installs from Settings, no PC and no FBI needed. It also fixes a crash when the console is turned off during a recording, and New 3DS games restarting the console after the app.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5: the update from inside the app (CIA, the module swapped and restarted, a dropped Wi-Fi connection, Cancel), power-off during a recording, Mario Kart 7 with a CTRPF plugin. The New 3DS fixes come from the statistics and your reports. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.6.0\n\n- Updates from the app (Settings → App → Updates). When the app opens with Wi-Fi it checks for a newer version; a dot on Settings shows one, with what is new in your language. Update downloads and installs it, Restart opens the new version, and the recorder restarts with it (the .3dsx: close it and open it again). A dropped connection goes on from where it stopped. Every update is signed by the developer and each file is checked before anything is installed. The check sends nothing about you or the console; switch Check Automatically off to check only when you press Check Now. Not while a recording runs.\n\n  This one last time, install 1.7.0 by hand (FBI, or the QR code below). Every version after it comes through the app.\n\n- Fixed: the console crashed when turned off during a recording wi...\n\n----------\n\nv1.6.0 (2026-11-22)\n3DS Recorder 1.6.0 fixes games crashing on a New 3DS after the app was opened, and frozen video in CTGP-7.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5 (Mario Kart 7 with a CTRPF plugin, Kirby: Planet Robobot, Pokémon Ultra Moon, HOME Menu). The New 3DS memory fix was confirmed by a tester: Pokémon Ultra Moon now starts with the New 3DS's full memory after the app, and recorded through a dozen restarts without a lost frame. The other New 3DS fixes come from the statistics and your reports. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.5.0\n\n- New 3DS: fixed games crashing or hanging at start after 3DS Recorder was opened (#24, #30). After the app closed, the system kept the next game's memory at 64 MB. Games made for the New 3DS's larger memory then crashed or hung at start: Smash Bros, Pokémon Sun / Moon / Ultra Sun / Ultra Moon, Monster Hunter 4 Ultimate / X, Minecraft: New 3DS Edition, The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth. The app no longer lowers that memory. When another app leaves it lowered (seen after 3DShell and CTGP-7), the recorder puts it back as soon as that app closes.\n- New 3DS: fixed the video freezing a few seconds into CTGP-7 (#25). Mario Kart 7's picture lies in a part of the memory the recorder used to skip.\n- Old 3DS: more frames in Monster Hunter 4G, Smash Bros and Pokémon Ultra Moon. In these games the recorder lives in the launche...\n\n----------\n\nv1.5.0 (2026-11-19)\n3DS Recorder now speaks ten languages, records faster on an Old 3DS, works next to HOME Menu battery mods, and can leave recordings unconverted until you download them.\n\nTested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5 in Monster Hunter 4G, Smash Bros, Pokémon Ultra Moon, Kirby and Mario Kart 7. This release has not been tried on a New 3DS yet. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new since 1.4.0\n\n- Ten languages: English, Українська, Deutsch, Español, Français, Italiano, Português (Brazil), 日本語, 简体中文 and 繁體中文.\n  - The first run offers the console's own language.\n  - All languages fit on one screen in the language list.\n  - The phone page follows the app's language; the converter page for computers follows the browser's.\n  - Japanese and Chinese have their own fonts, loaded only while that language is on.\n- Fixed: battery percentage mods for HOME Menu showed \"Error\" while the recorder ran (#10). The notification LED now goes through the system's own LED service, so the recorder no longer keeps the console's MCU connection to itself.\n- Convert To MP4: Automatically or On Download (#16). With On Download the app leaves .r3d files alone and converts a recording only when you send it to a phone (Settings → App).\n- Bottom Screen FPS (#18). With both screens recorded, the bottom one can be captured at 15, 10, 5 or 1 fps, leaving more of an Old 3DS to the top s...",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/BolgarMaxym97/3ds-recorder"
      }
    },
