      "info": {
        "title": "tougelike-3ds-pub",
        "author": "njlent",
        "description": "Tougelike for Nintendo 3DS: a night racing roguelike on Japanese mountain roads. Downloads (CIA and 3DSX), changelog and screenshots.",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "v0.1.71",
        "license": "NOASSERTION",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-25 at 21:17 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "v0.1.71 (2026-11-25)\nTougelike for Nintendo 3DS is the night racing roguelike on Japanese mountain roads, ported from the web game to the 3DS systems. Race down touge passes in the dark, drift through the bends, weave through traffic, take down rivals and bosses, and build every run from module drafts. It runs on the Old 3DS, 2DS and New 3DS, 2DS. - tougelike.com\n\nWhat's new\n\nSummary since 3DS 00.01.69\n\n- New: when a new version is out, the title screen says so. UPDATE in its menu installs it over the CIA or the 3DSX, then restarts the game, and your saves stay where they are. It needs Wi-Fi, and OPTIONS, GAME, CHECK FOR UPDATES turns it off.\n- New: the HOME Menu banner is an animated 3D scene of the HACHI 86 driving under the Tougelike logo.\n\n3DS 00.01.71\n\n- The HOME Menu banner is now a 3D scene of the HACHI 86 driving under the Tougelike logo, seen from all round. It boosts away with a blue exhaust flame, and its exhaust pops.\n\n3DS 00.01.70\n\n- When a new version is out, the title screen says so and an orange UPDATE row appears in its menu. The game asks once after it starts, only in the menus and never during a race. OPTIONS, GAME, CHECK FOR UPDATES turns it off.\n- UPDATE downloads the new version and installs it over the HOME Menu version or over tougelike.3dsx from the Homebrew Launcher, then starts the game again. The download is checked against the release's checksum before anything changes, and your saves stay where they are.\n\nDownloads\n\n| File | For | Size | SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- | --- |...\n\n----------\n\nv0.1.69 (2026-11-24)\nTougelike for Nintendo 3DS is the night racing roguelike on Japanese mountain roads, ported from the web game to the 3DS systems. Race down touge passes in the dark, drift through the bends, weave through traffic, take down rivals and bosses, and build every run from module drafts. It runs on the Old 3DS, 2DS and New 3DS, 2DS. - tougelike.com\n\nWhat's new\n\nSummary since 3DS 00.01.67\n\n- Fixed: a rare freeze in busy races that only the power button got you out of.\n- Fixed: road and rock textures smearing into streaks at the sides and bottom of the screen a few kilometres into a run.\n- The title screen and the CHANGELOG screen give tougelike.com for bug reports and ideas.\n\n3DS 00.01.69\n\n- A busy race could freeze the whole console, and only the power button got you out. A rare mix of what was on screen stopped the 3DS's graphics chip. A n3DS has since driven the same busy late-game descent 20 times in a row without a freeze.\n- A few kilometres into a run, road and rock textures at the sides and bottom of the screen no longer smear into streaks.\n\n3DS 00.01.68\n\n- The title screen and the CHANGELOG screen now give tougelike.com for bug reports and ideas, in place of njlent.de/games/tougelike.\n\nDownloads\n\n| File | For | Size | SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| tougelike.cia | HOME Menu, installed with FBI | 50.0 MB | 124a261dfbc7a6ac78c0386fdec02eae022f28da3dd74a8394c9733eb3c80f76 |\n| tougelike.3dsx | Homebrew Launcher | 49.8 MB | efd51d3a7b3198658ffa1f0763c6f7d8cbc604f5ac587a3bf...\n\n----------\n\nv0.1.67 (2026-11-19)\nTougelike for Nintendo 3DS is the night racing roguelike on Japanese mountain roads, ported from the web game to the 3DS and 2DS. Race down touge passes in the dark, drift through the bends, weave through traffic, take down rivals and bosses, and build every run from module drafts. It runs on the Old 3DS, 2DS and New 3DS, 2DS. - tougelike.com\n\nWhat's new\n\nSummary since 3DS 00.01.57\n\n- About 8% more steps a second on a n3DS/n2DS: SMOOTH FRAMES now starts off (adds ~4 fps).\n- Shorter stalls. Late in a long run the longest one went from 1.3 seconds to 0.4 at o3DS speed, and getting a long-played save ready to write from 1.2 seconds to under 0.4.\n- Fixed: running out of memory with a long-played save in OPTIONS, SAVE and in the garage.\n- Fixed: a o3DS stalling every 600 frames while the game wrote its log.\n- Drafts, route choices and part offers show your CONDITION, so you can judge a repair before you pick.\n\n3DS 00.01.67\n\n- Drafts, route choices and part offers show your CONDITION at the top right, beside your chips, so you can see how much a repair would help before you pick.\n- SPOOL's multiplier is boost blue, as in the web game.\n- The combo's timer bar sits clear below its number instead of touching it, and the HAIRPIN warning under it moved down to make room.\n\n3DS 00.01.66\n\n- Leaving the garage with a long-played save could run out of memory. When memory is short, the game now clears it up before it saves, which on an o3DS adds about half a second to the save.\n\n3DS 00.01.65...",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/njlent/tougelike-3ds-pub"
      }
    }
  ]
}